Z||000000||JamesWM83||07-20-2001||01:16 AM||||How much would it cost to put a new rod in one of these engines? And what else should I put in it for performance while I'm at it? I'm on low budget until I can find a co-signer for a loan. Thanks. <P>~James||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||07-20-2001||06:09 PM||||your going to have to take the intake off to put new rods in.  that wouldnt be too hard or expensive but if you have a knocking rod then you probably need more then just new rods.  <P>you could probably do it for a hundred bucks.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||07-20-2001||06:28 PM||||If in fact you have a rod knock the rod bearing has too much play (hence the knock) and needs to be replaced.<P>The problem is that rod knock usually is a symptom (result?) of poor lubrication so as Formula implies you're looking at more than replacing a few rods.  A more practical fix would more likely start off with replacing all the bearings.  If one is worn the others probably aren't in much better shape. <BR>||||reg||1
